Speedmine Session Log
=====================
Date: 2026-06-15

## Changes Made

### 1. Insta-rebreak render loop (onRenderWorld)
- Every Render3DEvent frame, for each MiningData in miningQueue where hasAttemptedBreak() == true:
  - Skips if clientState.isAir(), fluid is present, or hardness == -1.0f (unbreakable).
  - Sends START_DESTROY_BLOCK + STOP_DESTROY_BLOCK + HandSwingC2SPacket every frame.
  - Resets swapBackTicks = swapBackTicksConfig.get() each frame to keep the tool swap
    alive until the server confirms the break via BlockUpdateS2CPacket.
- Previously only sent STOP_DESTROY_BLOCK (bare STOP is silently ignored by server-side
  block-break trackers without a preceding START — this was the root cause of slowness).

### 2. Instant-breakable block fast path (onAttackBlock)
- When calcBlockBreakingDelta(blockState, world, pos) >= 1.0f (best hotbar tool):
  - Cancels the event (bypasses vanilla's blockBreakingCooldown gate).
  - Silent-swaps to the best hotbar tool via swapTo() + swapBackTicks tracking.
  - Sends START_DESTROY_BLOCK + STOP_DESTROY_BLOCK + HandSwing immediately.
  - Does NOT queue into miningQueue — bypasses the full packet-mine path.
- Previously did not cancel the event, relying on vanilla's attackBlock which was
  blocked by blockBreakingCooldown from prior packet-mine activity.

### 3. BPS counter
- Fields: bpsCount (int), bpsWindowStart (long).
- Incremented in handleBlockUpdatePacket when a server-confirmed air update matches
  a miningQueue entry that had hasAttemptedBreak() == true.
- Outputs via warning(): "[Speedmine] BPS: X" once per second.
- Reset to 0 on onActivate, onDeactivate, and onGameLeft.

### 4. DAMAGE mode reactive swap
- Completely isolated from PACKET mode swap tracking (own fields: damageSwappedToSlot,
  damageOriginalSlot).
- Reactive: swaps to best tool while breakingProgress > 0 and looking at valid block;
  calls damageSwapBack() immediately when not digging or target is gone.
- Uses module's own getBestTool() (raw getMiningSpeedMultiplier scan) — not InvUtils
  which gates on isSuitableFor and conflicted with global InvUtils.previousSlot state.

### 5. Swap-back tick default reduced from 3 to 1
- Since swapBackTicks is now refreshed every render frame during active insta-rebreak,
  the swap stays alive until the block is confirmed broken. 1 tick after confirmation
  is sufficient.

### 6. damageSwapConfig setting
- New EnumSetting<Swap> "damage-auto-swap" visible only in DAMAGE mode.
- NORMAL / SILENT / OFF — mirrors PACKET mode's auto-swap.

### 7. swapBackTicksConfig setting
- New IntSetting "swap-back-ticks" (default 1, range 1-20) replacing the hardcoded 3.
- All four swapBackTicks = 3 assignments replaced with swapBackTicksConfig.get().

## Key Decisions

- START+STOP per frame (not just STOP): Required because vanilla server-side break
  tracking requires a START before it will process a STOP. Bare STOP spam was being
  silently dropped.
- swapBackTicks refresh in render loop: Prevents premature swap-back while server
  hasn't confirmed the break, which was causing subsequent STOP packets to arrive with
  the wrong server-side slot.
- Module's own getBestTool vs InvUtils.findFastestTool: Meteor's version gates on
  isSuitableFor, skipping tools that have higher speed multipliers but wrong tag type.
  Module's version uses raw getMiningSpeedMultiplier which is more aggressive.
- Isolated DAMAGE swap fields: InvUtils.previousSlot is a global static clobbered by
  other modules (AutoTotem etc.), causing "sometimes doesn't switch" failures.

## Compile Status
All changes compile cleanly: ./gradlew compileJava → BUILD SUCCESSFUL
